course: dictionary
lesson: 7584
title: Stopping problems before they start
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prevention is a noun. It means stopping something bad from happening before it happens. The word is built from prevent, to stop something from happening, plus -ion, which turns it into a thing you can name.
explain: Read the example sentence and look at the words after the colon: «Prevention is simple: stay on paths, wear shoes and long trousers in the bush or desert, look before you put hands under rocks and logs, and shake out shoes and clothes left outside.» Each step is a way of stopping a bad thing, like a snake bite or a sting, before it can hurt you.
explain: Now try the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word: «Stopping something bad from happening before it happens is simple.» It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Prevention means stopping something bad from happening before it happens.
fact: Fire prevention includes smoke alarms and not playing with matches.
fact: Illness prevention includes washing your hands and having vaccines.
fact: «Prevention is better than cure» means it is easier to stop a problem than to fix it later.
fact: Other phrases use it too: crime prevention, accident prevention, injury prevention, and prevention of accidents.
exercise: What does prevention mean? | Fixing a problem after it has already happened | Something that makes accidents more likely | *Stopping something bad from happening before it happens
exercise: What does the saying «Prevention is better than cure» mean? | Cures always work, so you never need to stop anything | *It is easier to stop a problem than to fix it later | Doctors are better than medicine
exercise: Which is an example of fire prevention? | Playing with matches in the garden | *Keeping smoke alarms working | Leaving clothes near a heater
test: The advice of RoSPA is never to go onto ice on ponds, lakes, rivers or canals. What is the prevention here? | Skating on the ice with a helmet on | Walking on the ice very slowly | *Staying off the ice so people do not get hurt
test: Which of these is an example of illness prevention? | Staying in bed until you feel better | *Washing your hands before you eat | Eating sweets all day
exam: Jayden reads «Prevention is simple: stay on paths, wear shoes and long trousers in the bush or desert.» What is the main idea of the sentence? | Walking in the bush is always dangerous | Deserts are the best place to walk | *Taking simple steps now to stop harm before it happens | Shoes and trousers are only for the desert
